  "body": "Fixes #313942\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\nThe default workspace window size (1440×900) introduced in #262266 was never clamped to the display work area. On displays where the work area height is less than 900px logical pixels (e.g. 1366×768 laptops, or 1920×1080 at 125% DPI scaling), the new window overflows the visible area — pushing the title bar above the screen and/or the status bar behind the taskbar.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\nSwitch new window positioning from `displayToUse.bounds` to `displayToUse.workArea` and clamp the default width/height to fit within the actual visible area.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\nVerified on a 1920×1080 display at 125% DPI scaling — new window now opens fully within bounds with both title bar and status bar accessible.\r\n",
  "rebaseable": true
 },
