   "body": "@benibenj thanks for consolidating #317762 into #313942, and for the note that this PR\r\nresolves both paths.\r\n\r\nQuick summary of the change in case it is useful:\r\n\r\n- Clamps the default window size and position to `displayToUse.workArea` instead of\r\n  `displayToUse.bounds`, falling back to `bounds` when `workArea` reports zero, which can\r\n  happen on Linux/X11.\r\n- Bounds the `ensureNoOverlap()` offset loop to the same work area, so the repeated +30\r\n  offset cannot push the chrome back outside the visible region.\r\n- 30 lines in one file, `windowsStateHandler.ts`. No new dependencies, no API changes.\r\n\r\nVerified on a dual-monitor Windows 11 setup at 125% scaling, with the source window both\r\nmaximized and not.\r\n\r\nThe workflows are still awaiting approval so CI has not run yet. Happy to rework anything\r\nif the approach needs changing, and equally happy to wait if it is simply queued.\r\n",
