  {
   "sha": "472754d53b29cb86be91f31c692a584e2b891b33",
   "node_id": "C_kwDOSQgfWNoAKDQ3Mjc1NGQ1M2IyOWNiODZiZTkxZjMxYzY5MmE1ODRlMmI4OTFiMzM",
   "commit": {
    "author": {
     "name": "mx-92x",
     "email": "96252981+mx-92x@users.noreply.github.com",
     "date": "2026-07-29T12:57:01Z"
    },
    "committer": {
     "name": "mx-92x",
     "email": "96252981+mx-92x@users.noreply.github.com",
     "date": "2026-07-29T13:17:38Z"
    },
    "message": "Keep default window offset inside the display work area\n\nensureNoOverlap() offsets a new window by 30px whenever it shares an x or y\ncoordinate with an existing window, but it never checked the result against\nthe display work area. Displays arranged side by side share the same vertical\norigin, so default-positioned windows on a second display collide on y\nrepeatedly and the accumulated offset pushes the title bar above the screen\nand the status bar behind the taskbar.\n\nPass the work area into ensureNoOverlap() and stop offsetting once the window\nwould no longer fit inside it.",
    "tree": {
     "sha": "e3c37e20c899144e5fb5bbc8354b58f513f0063f",
     "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode/git/trees/e3c37e20c899144e5fb5bbc8354b58f513f0063f"
